        "timestamp": 1794939026
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"thumbs up\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f44d\" role=\"img\" title=\"thumbs up\">:thumbs_up:</span> cfallin submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15330#pullrequestreview-5944174977\">PR review</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Thanks!</p>\n<p>Simple change, nice speedup, looks great.</p>\n<p>Only a minor nit: we try to avoid <code>as T</code> integer casts since they silently truncate (here unlikely/impossible due to input-size limits but we keep the general rule to make audits easier). Can you use <code>u32::try_from(...).expect(...)</code> and likewise for <code>usize</code> here? Happy to merge once that's changed.</p>\n</blockquote>",
